   edge [
      id 0
      source 0
      target 1
      tip_text "make your own sandwich: tuna salad on country white bread, cheddar, lettuce, tomato, cucumber, mayo. yuuuum."
   ]
   edge [
      id 1
      source 0
      target 218
      tip_text "Get the superman roll. Tuna avocado sala is also great."
   ]
   edge [
      id 2
      source 0
      target 254
      tip_text "super cute and inviting during the day. i recommend eggs florentine with crispy bacon on the side for brunch."
   ]
   edge [
      id 3
      source 0
      target 301
      tip_text "really fantastic choices for brunch! try something you normally wouldn't."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4
      source 0
      target 820
      tip_text "used to stand on this line everyday before the commute to midtown for the much-needed coffee w. milk and sugar"
   ]
   edge [
      id 5
      source 0
      target 851
      tip_text "whitefish salad on a freshly made bagel. the long line is worth it, but move quickly, know your order, and never *ever* ask to have your bagel toasted (they're freshly made on premises!)"
   ]
   edge [
      id 6
      source 0
      target 1079
      tip_text "can't get enough of the avocado panini on sourdough, w\/ home fries on the side, and of course, a cup of mud."
   ]
   edge [
      id 7
      source 0
      target 1264
      tip_text "brunch served until 5pm!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 8
      source 0
      target 1598
      tip_text "bacon wrapped dates, fried goat cheese, pulled pork empanadas, even the brussel sprouts are good!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 9
      source 0
      target 1628
      tip_text "Go to Angelina Cafe and eat a steak sandwich."
   ]
   edge [
      id 10
      source 0
      target 2073
      tip_text "soup + 1\/2 sandwich combo for lunch!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 11
      source 0
      target 2380
      tip_text "my recs: avocado, tomato, cucumber salad. avocado + shrimp + cucumber appetizer. avocado and chicken sandwich. notice a pattern here?"
   ]
   edge [
      id 12
      source 0
      target 2474
      tip_text "oysters and steak and wine and happiness"
   ]
   edge [
      id 13
      source 0
      target 2570
      tip_text "royale with cheese. and chips with onion dip."
   ]
   edge [
      id 14
      source 0
      target 2589
      tip_text "all these hipsters can't be wrong! this place has a great brunch - everything is fresh and pretty cheap too! super long lines so sit at the bar if you don't mind."
   ]
   edge [
      id 15
      source 0
      target 2607
      tip_text "keep it basic with eggs, bacon, and a side salad -you won't be disappointed"
   ]
   edge [
      id 16
      source 0
      target 2690
      tip_text "Sunday brunch special: coffee, OJ, bloody mary, baked eggs, side of bacon. Happy."
   ]
   edge [
      id 17
      source 0
      target 2704
      tip_text "no wifi\/power on the weekends."
   ]
   edge [
      id 18
      source 0
      target 2738
      tip_text "highlights: marble soda, pork curry, and The Bathroom."
   ]
   edge [
      id 19
      source 0
      target 2763
      tip_text "Oysters are bland. Meh."
   ]
   edge [
      id 20
      source 0
      target 2952
      tip_text "eurotart. fruit, coconut flakes, and brownie bites. oh my."
   ]
   edge [
      id 21
      source 0
      target 2996
      tip_text "no cell phones at the counter!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 22
      source 0
      target 2996
      tip_text "$4.20 for a latte. oh baristas, you so funny."
   ]
   edge [
      id 23
      source 0
      target 3053
      tip_text "young baby coconut. drink the deliciousness, then ask for it to be split open and eat the insides. goodbye hangover!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 24
      source 0
      target 3066
      tip_text "the roast beef sandwich is pretty much my version of lunch heaven."
   ]
   edge [
      id 25
      source 0
      target 3237
      tip_text "surprisingly great bacon - add it to your egg &amp; cheese in the morning!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 26
      source 0
      target 3353
      tip_text "honey dew melon with tapioca - yum"
   ]
   edge [
      id 27
      source 0
      target 3518
      tip_text "don't mess with the mayor"
   ]
   edge [
      id 28
      source 0
      target 3552
      tip_text "Petisco's Eggs + French Toast. fatfatfat."
   ]
   edge [
      id 29
      source 0
      target 3820
      tip_text "egg salad sandwich on toasted rye! pickle on the side."
   ]
   edge [
      id 30
      source 0
      target 3895
      tip_text "Glorious Belgian waffle truck - on Astor Pl near NYU every Tues and Thurs night."
   ]
   edge [
      id 31
      source 0
      target 4553
      tip_text "if meat is on the menu, eat it"
   ]
   edge [
      id 32
      source 0
      target 5124
      tip_text "Danny, the cute ex-hockey player turned bartender, no longer works here. Don't embarrass yourself by asking about him."
   ]
   edge [
      id 33
      source 0
      target 5363
      tip_text "best brunch in the hood - definitely get the biscuits w\/ homemade jam to start, slow whisked scrambled eggs with bacon, and the deliciously fresh green salad. top it off with a cucumber mint spritzer!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 34
      source 2
      target 3
      tip_text "The calamari as an appetizer and the quail. Pretty good, if a bit rich. The berry and creme desert thing was really, really good!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 35
      source 2
      target 719
      tip_text "Best catfish in NYC"
   ]
   edge [
      id 36
      source 2
      target 1069
      tip_text "My tip is to order something on the menu, exactly as it is. No matter what you order, it will show up perfectly cooked and taste amazing. Just trust 'em, they know better than you do."
   ]
   edge [
      id 37
      source 2
      target 1176
      tip_text "Pulled pork sandwich. Don't spoil it by adding or removing anything. It's awesome!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 38
      source 2
      target 1743
      tip_text "Have anything with the word pulled and you'll go away happy!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 39
      source 4
      target 3
      tip_text "Be careful with the napkins on your pants. They leave remnants behind. As in lint."
   ]
   edge [
