      tip_text "Come hungry for lunch specials. You will get a lot of food. Chirashi bowl and sura tanmen is very satisfying here."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4759
      source 726
      target 5782
      tip_text "Get Turkish tea - it goes well with pretty much everything. Really friendly staff here."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4760
      source 726
      target 6166
      tip_text "Baguette was too hard for my taste."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4761
      source 728
      target 729
      tip_text "$5 apps at happy hour = great deal"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4762
      source 728
      target 4867
      tip_text "Classic burger. No frills. Worth braving a few tourists and a less bro-heavy ambiance than 3rd ave. bartenders downstairs are fabulous."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4763
      source 728
      target 4867
      tip_text "I'm shocked at the number of bad tips here. This is false. Yes, it gets crowded and the service can get overwhelmed, but that's par for the course with any famous NYC jaunt. Come on a quiet night."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4764
      source 730
      target 729
      tip_text "Have an Abita Amber after upgrading your cable box at Time Warner a few blocks away"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4765
      source 730
      target 800
      tip_text "Try the 14oz and have the carrot cake."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4766
      source 731
      target 729
      tip_text "Crab cake sandwich is AMAZING."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4767
      source 731
      target 4485
      tip_text "The Mediterranean vege burger with dill dressing was quite tasty! Affordable &amp; quick, too."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4768
      source 733
      target 732
      tip_text "Filet mignon melts in your mouth. And please please PLEASE get the chocolate bread pudding. The best I've ever had. You can also get chocolate \/ banana bread pudding half and half"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4769
      source 733
      target 5041
      tip_text "Special pork buns!!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4770
      source 735
      target 734
      tip_text "Try sitting at the bar and not ordering off the menu - let the team decide your menu for you."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4771
      source 735
      target 5424
      tip_text "Some of the most beautiful (and delicious) Japanese food you'll ever eat."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4772
      source 736
      target 734
      tip_text "Swiss chard tortellini are to die for."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4773
      source 736
      target 1109
      tip_text "Food is satisfying - great pancakes and fresh juices. Service leaves something to be desired but the prices are right for a regular breakfast spot."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4774
      source 736
      target 2516
      tip_text "Definitely not pasta made in house and food is just alright. Very midtown crowd. Good service though."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4775
      source 738
      target 737
      tip_text "Very very very happy with the branzino."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4776
      source 738
      target 1920
      tip_text "Very reasonable wine by the glass selection."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4777
      source 738
      target 2694
      tip_text "Ricotta w\/figs and honey. Every time. And the little table at the far end of the bar."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4778
      source 738
      target 2970
      tip_text "2 squares, to go, 3 napkins, to eat in the parking lot."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4779
      source 738
      target 3048
      tip_text "Please don't come here. So I can."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4780
      source 740
      target 739
      tip_text "Go and have the Spicy Crispy Shrimp!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4781
      source 740
      target 739
      tip_text "Do not miss the Spicy Crispy Shrimp or the Big Eye Tuna Tarts. My favorite is the Tuna Crispy Rice. Make sure to sit at the sushi bar at least once."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4782
      source 740
      target 945
      tip_text "Avoid the Phaalbat all costs. It might kill you."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4783
      source 740
      target 2407
      tip_text "Do not miss this New York (Brooklyn) gem! Perhaps the best pizza on the planet. Get the plain pie first..you'll have a second one for sure and can add the mushrooms then!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4784
      source 740
      target 2517
      tip_text "Don't miss this BBQ joint. Outstanding food, great atmosphere, and awesome Banana Pudding!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4785
      source 740
      target 3274
      tip_text "try the homemade pastas at this hidden NYC gem!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4786
      source 741
      target 739
      tip_text "Big Eye Tuna Tarts will change your life"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4787
      source 741
      target 1064
      tip_text "Soup dumplings"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4788
      source 741
      target 2106
      tip_text "don't wait 2 hours for this pizza, it's really not worth it"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4789
      source 741
      target 3054
      tip_text "definitely get the chana masala"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4790
      source 741
      target 5209
      tip_text "The dessert gelato wasn't any good. $8 for melted gelato, 4 strawberries and sugar isn't worth it. The rest of the food was great, sea scallops with crabmeat was delicious."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4791
      source 742
      target 739
      tip_text "Best. Bloody May. Ever."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4792
      source 743
      target 739
      tip_text "the lobster tempura is a must!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4793
      source 743
      target 1198
      tip_text "You HAVE to try the eggs benedict with apples on french toast..make sure you ask for bacon so the sweetness evens out..it sounds weird but its seriously amazing!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4794
      source 743
      target 4802
      tip_text "Try the pink starburst off the secret menu..just ask! So good!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4795
      source 744
      target 739
      tip_text "Alright food actually but don't expect any attention from the staff. Not even standing up waving the menu seemed to help."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4796
      source 744
      target 1350
      tip_text "Whaley Burger w fried egg, red beet and pineapple. Ozzie style!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4797
      source 744
      target 1879
      tip_text "That's actually one of the worse burgers I've had. Pity, they seem so nice. BLT was quite soggy too."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4798
      source 744
      target 3274
      tip_text "Rustic. Not fancy but good. Quick and friendly"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4799
      source 746
      target 745
      tip_text "Let them just bring out the goodness! They know what they are doing."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4800
      source 746
      target 1674
      tip_text "Start with the spinach salad. It's delicious."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4801
      source 746
      target 2068
      tip_text "My current favorite steakhouse in the city. I say get the Rib Eye over the sirloin or the filet. Amazing, complete with Flintstone-esque protruding bone. ; )"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4802
      source 746
      target 2992
      tip_text "FYI: No bathroom is kind of a bummer. Other than that perfection."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4803
      source 746
      target 3484
      tip_text "They just redesigned the place so now there's plenty of space. Best pizza in this hood."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4804
      source 746
      target 4136
      tip_text "Ground beef hardshell tacos. Do it."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4805
      source 748
      target 747
      tip_text "Oh and oil on table >>>>>"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4806
      source 748
      target 1722
      tip_text "The nicest baristas! They are always on point with their Iced Tea Lemonades!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4807
      source 748
      target 3799
      tip_text "Nicer Baristas"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4808
      source 749
      target 747
      tip_text "Try the Ciabatta Con Pollo Sandwich!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4809
      source 750
      target 751
      tip_text "Tasting menu with wine pairing was perfect. Amazing desserts!!! Lychee sorbet, wheat germ ice cream, and chocolate soufflé drools."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4810
      source 750
      target 1249
      tip_text "Apple crumb foie gras, lobster, and sea scallops were amazing! Finish off with Brooklyn Bridge dessert."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4811
      source 750
      target 5355
      tip_text "Happy hour! Shrimp corndog and lobster slider!"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4812
      source 752
      target 753
      tip_text "if you are a college student in the area, it's a PERFECT place to go before getting dropped off by parents. Otherwise, make sure to go there during Brooklyn Restaurant Week for a massive feast for $25"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4813
      source 752
      target 1725
      tip_text "Good place for take-out, or an affordable hour or two to hang out with friends. I was a big fan of their burritos and quesadillas here but everything is pretty good. Outdoor dining's great in Spring."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4814
      source 752
      target 1807
      tip_text "Not as good and more expensive than John's Coffee Shop but has a lot more of a New York atmosphere with signed images of news anchors and foreign currency on the wall. Owner is really talkative too"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4815
      source 752
      target 1877
      tip_text "Thin crust, more of a traditional Italian style pie like you'd find at Lombardi's or Grimaldi's. Tried the Arugula Pie as per Food Network's Ted Allen's suggestion, it was good but sausage is the best"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4816
      source 752
      target 2123
      tip_text "Expect to wait maybe fifteen minutes, but worth it, the BLT is a must, along with their chicken paninis. Place is small and crowded, so don't expect to be able to eat in. Expensive but worth it."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4817
      source 752
      target 3604
      tip_text "One of my favorite cheap eats in New York City, decor has a weird mix between traditional Japanese art and baseball. Order a Grand Slam Curry and split it, really great food and unlike anything else."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4818
      source 752
      target 4258
      tip_text "a great place to pair with a trip to the Botanical Gardens or Brooklyn Museum. Line is large on a Saturday, if you can, go on a week day. Pancakes and grits are the highlight here but lots to choose."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4819
      source 752
      target 4305
      tip_text "Portions here are giant, the place often has beggars by the door but food's good. Don't bother with the restaurant portion, prices are way higher there with same take-out food. Make sure to call ahead"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4820
      source 752
      target 4406
      tip_text "This was a favorite place of one of my Thai friends. Always order the Thai Iced Tea and the Banana Sundae is a lot of fun. Definitely better than Thai 101 and they do take-out too which is great."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4821
      source 752
      target 4430
      tip_text "Great selection of cream cheeses and variety of bagels, I liked the blueberry cream cheese and cinnamon raisin bagels the best. Try ordering a burger or egg sandwich here, have bagel halves for bread."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4822
      source 752
      target 4728
      tip_text "a bit of a walk if you're a Pratt Student but worth it. Fish n' Chips and Shepard's Pies are easy recommendations and deep fried pizza is interesting. Food goes half price on special during Happy Hour"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4823
      source 752
      target 4793
      tip_text "If you're getting food here, go for the Tacos or the Bowls. Their rice and beans are nothing special, so the best strategy is to load up on sour cream and meat."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4824
      source 752
      target 5549
      tip_text "For most intents and purposes, if you are looking for something special, go across the street to Junior's, otherwise this is still a fun place to go with friends. Order the 2,000 calorie cookie desert"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4825
      source 752
      target 5613
      tip_text "Likely to be one of the first places you go to at Pratt. It's really good until you go to their sister location, The 3 Luigi's which is located a few blocks away. Still great and fast, a bit oily."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4826
      source 754
      target 753
      tip_text "what a lovely cheesecake! see ya next vacation :*"
   ]
   edge [
      id 4827
      source 755
      target 753
      tip_text "I can't get over the rat that was seen on top of the cheesecakes a couple years ago. Google it please. If that's what their secret crack ingredient is count me out! no matter how good they are."
   ]
   edge [
      id 4828
      source 756
      target 753
      tip_text "Try the matzo ball soup: _perfect_ from the chicken soup to the matzoh ball"
   ]
   edge [
